IMPORT prelude

-- Children and Young Persons Act 1993 (Singapore) -- who is a child or young person (s 2), when a child is in need of care or
-- protection (s 5), ill-treatment (s 6), contributing to delinquency (s 7) and sexual exploitation (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CYPA1993.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 30 of 2019 shown in force (the extended definition of "young person" from 30 December 2025). The section numbers are the
-- body's.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 16 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the protective definitions and the
-- offences against children. Not encoded: the powers to remove and the care and protection orders (Part 3 procedure), the Youth
-- Court and youth offenders (Parts 4 to 6), homes and institutions, the guardianship and fostering provisions, and the
-- publication restrictions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Children and Young Persons Act 1993 -- protection`

§§ `2 -- definitions`

-- s 2: "child" means a person "below 14 years of age"; "young person" means "14 years of age or older but below 18 years of age"
-- (raised from 16 by Act 30 of 2019, in force 30 December 2025).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the person's status under the Act` MEANS
    IF `age` LESS THAN 14 THEN "child"
    ELSE IF `age` LESS THAN 18 THEN "young person" ELSE "adult"

§§ `5 -- in need of care or protection`

-- s 5(1): a child or young person is in need of care or protection on any of the listed grounds, including: (a) no parent or
-- guardian; (b) abandoned and the parent cannot be found; (c) the parent cannot or does not provide necessities or proper
-- supervision; (d) ill-treated or at risk, by the parent or by another whom the parent does not protect against; (e) medical
-- treatment needed and refused; (f) harmful behaviour the parent cannot remedy; (g) emotional harm from the parent's emotional or
-- psychological abuse; (h) a relevant offence in the household; (i) destitute, begging, illegal activities, or inhaling
-- intoxicants. (2): emotional abuse includes persistent rejection or degradation, threats, isolation, confinement in a small space
-- for discipline, encouraging maladaptive behaviour, and exposure to violence against a "related person".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `no parent or guardian`
    `abandoned and parent cannot be found`
    `parent neglects necessities`
    `ill-treated by parent`
    `at risk from another and parent will not protect`
    `parent refuses needed medical treatment`
    `confined in a small space as discipline`
    `exposed to violence against a related person`
    `found begging`
    `parents divorcing`
    `strict but loving parent`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is in need of care or protection` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `parents divorcing` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `strict but loving parent` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6 -- ill-treatment`

-- s 6(1): a person with "custody, charge or care" of a child or young person commits an offence if they ill-treat the child or
-- "cause, procure or KNOWINGLY PERMIT" another to do so. (2)(a): A knowingly permits ill-treatment by C if A "knows or has REASON
-- TO BELIEVE" the child was at risk from C and failed to take the steps A "could reasonably have been expected in A's circumstances
-- to take"; (b) those circumstances include A's own experience of being ill-treated by C.
-- (4): a parent who wilfully or unreasonably neglects to provide adequate food, clothing, medical aid, lodging or care is DEEMED to
-- have neglected the child in a manner likely to cause harm.
-- (5): conviction is possible even if another person prevented the harm, or the child died.
-- (6): up to 14 years and $40,000 if death is caused; otherwise up to 8 years and $8,000.
DECLARE Carer HAS
    `has custody, charge or care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ill-treated the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable steps to protect` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the carer` IS A Carer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carer commits a section 6 offence` IF
        `the carer`'s `has custody, charge or care`
    AND (    `the carer`'s `ill-treated the child`
         OR  (`the carer`'s `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` AND (NOT `the carer`'s `took reasonable steps to protect`)))

GIVEN `death was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for ill-treatment` MEANS
    IF `death was caused` THEN 14 ELSE 8

§§ `7 -- contributing to delinquency`

-- s 7(1): causing or procuring a child or young person, or as carer allowing them, to be in a place for begging or illegal
-- activities -- $2,000 or 12 months. (2): if the carer allowed them to be there, it is PRESUMED to be for that purpose unless the
-- contrary is proved.
GIVEN `the carer allowed the child to be there` IS A BOOLEAN, `the carer proved another purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `the child was there begging` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carer is taken to have allowed it for begging` IF
    `the child was there begging` AND `the carer allowed the child to be there` AND (NOT `the carer proved another purpose`)

§§ `8 -- sexual exploitation`

-- s 8(1): any obscene or indecent act with or by a child or young person BELOW 16 is an offence, whatever the consent.
-- (2), (3): for a young person aged 16 or 17, an offence only if (i) the young person did not consent, or (ii) the accused is in a
-- relationship that is EXPLOITATIVE of them -- and (5) consent need not be proved either way for (ii). (4): a good-faith mistaken
-- belief in consent is a defence to limb (i) only.
-- (8): exploitation is PRESUMED where the accused is a parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent (or their de facto partner),
-- a teacher at the young person's school, an established instructor, a custodial officer, a doctor, TCM practitioner or
-- psychologist treating them, or a lawyer or counsellor acting for them. (9): the presumption does not apply to a person lawfully
-- married to the young person.
-- (10), (11): up to 7 years where a child is involved, 5 where a young person; 10 and 7 for a repeat offender.
DECLARE Relationship IS ONE OF
    `step-parent`
    `teacher at their school`
    `their music teacher`
    `their doctor`
    `their lawyer`
    `spouse`
    `a peer`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A Relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exploitation is presumed` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `spouse` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a peer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `relationship is exploitative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an offence under section 8` IF
    IF `age` LESS THAN 16 THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `age` LESS THAN 18 THEN (NOT `consented`) OR `relationship is exploitative`
         ELSE FALSE

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years under section 8` MEANS
    IF `age` LESS THAN 14
    THEN (IF `repeat offender` THEN 10 ELSE 7)
    ELSE (IF `repeat offender` THEN 7 ELSE 5)
